{
 "esm": "1.0.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "SurfacePBLColumn",
  "description": "Surface + boundary-layer subassembly of the EqWeather reference suite (WRF em_scm_xy): the revised MM5 surface layer (components/atmospheric_dynamics/sfclayrev) and the YSU boundary layer (components/atmospheric_dynamics/ysu) mounted by reference as top-level systems and coupled in the WRF order with variable_map/param_to_var edges (esm-spec 10.4): the assembly's shared scalar state (SurfacePBLColumn.*) feeds both schemes, the surface layer's u*, psi_m, psi_h, Ri_b, wind speed, 10 m wind and z0 drive the PBL scheme, and every scheme output is exposed back as a SurfacePBLColumn variable so the assembly can be tested as a whole against the driver-level WRF dumps. The atmospheric column state (theta, u, v, qv, qc, qi, p, p_int, exner, ze, rthraten) enters YSU through its input_<x> rewrite targets via a template library injected at the mount edge (esm-spec 9.7.10), so one document holds one column state (one regime). NOT co-mounted: the slab land-surface scheme (components/land_surface/slab), which in WRF sits between sfclayrev and YSU and recomputes hfx/qfx/tsk -- its column grid is the same column_nonuniform_1d 'lev' axis at a different size (4 soil layers vs 59 model layers) and esm index sets are document-scoped, so the two cannot share a document (see PLAN.md gap (n)); the slab's fluxes are therefore prescribed (hfx_lsm, qfx_lsm) and the slab is assembled separately in surface_soil_column.esm. KNOWN BINDING LIMITATIONS (Rust CLI, 2026-09-06): (1) the mounted components' own inline tests are re-run inside this document under the coupling and fail there (their parameter overrides are displaced by the coupled values) -- run this file with `esm test --model SurfacePBLColumn`; (2) coupling endpoints inside a model that has subsystems evaluate to NaN, so the components cannot be hidden behind test-free wrapper models; repro data/eqwefic/esm-repro/assemblies/.",
  "license": "MIT",
  "tags": [
   "wrf",
   "eqweather",
   "assembly",
   "surface-layer",
   "pbl",
   "column"
  ],
  "references": [
   {
    "citation": "Skamarock, W. C., et al. (2021). A Description of the Advanced Research WRF Model Version 4.3. NCAR Tech. Note NCAR/TN-556+STR."
   }
  ]
 },
 "metaparameters": {
  "NLEV": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 59,
   "description": "Number of model layers of the mounted YSU column (bound at the Pbl mount edge; 59 = em_scm_xy). Declared here because the mounted document's grid import merges the axis lev with size NLEV into this document's registry."
  }
 },
 "index_sets": {
  "secant_steps": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": 33
  }
 },
 "models": {
  "Sfc": {
   "ref": "../components/atmospheric_dynamics/sfclayrev/sfclayrev.esm"
  },
  "Pbl": {
   "ref": "../components/atmospheric_dynamics/ysu/ysu.esm",
   "bindings": {
    "NLEV": "NLEV"
   },
   "expression_template_imports": [
    {
     "ref": "./tests/scm_step60_atmos_inputs.esm"
    }
   ]
  },
  "SurfacePBLColumn": {
